topics home +0.7 food +0.5 travel +0.4 work +0.3
styles comfort=generous gossip=careful refuse=plain tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sets a jar aside before counting the larder and remembers quiet charcoal smoke in the hills.

words
oath! = Crack my spare crock | Freeze my last crust
saying! = Count the shelf after sharing | Good lids beat grand labels
shelf = a stout upper plank | a level kitchen shelf
jar = a small stone jar | a squat preserving crock
grub = a warm loaf end | a slice fresh from the oven
seal = a clean wax lip | a tight plain lid
smoke = an uphill thread of smoke | a thin camp plume
walk = a good long circuit | a stretch beyond the dray road
snow = new snow on dark bark | a first white dusting
wind = a salt-heavy gust | a bite off the Sound
tea = a cup still steaming | a swallow at drinking heat
label = a dry paper strip | a scratched wooden tag
rest = a spell beside the hill path | a seat above the last cart
portion = a share already wrapped | a jar for another table

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Count me willing to share a jar even if the other shelf hasn't a penny on it.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A different House may bring a bright label. I'd look at the seal with my own eyes.
opinion @1 road for 1 : A long walk takes all sorts of noise out of one's ears before supper.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : An unknown traveller gets bread without access to my store key.
opinion @1 times against 1 [world.times=lean|hard] : A tight winter measures a cupboard by the mouths it actually feeds.
opinion @1 city mixed 1 : The Sump has food worth making and streets where a hillside would be very welcome.

grown
line @1 greet : I've kept a clean spot beside my shelf-end crock. | Come up beyond that salty draught.
line @1 greet.return : Your greeting's as welcome as a loaf fresh out.
line @1 again.open : Back before I tied the spare jar.
line @1 farewell : May your supper stretch to company.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll keep those wishes for the road uphill.
line @1 react.news : Let's hear what's come into town with the carts.
line @1 react.news.new : That hasn't earned a mark on my shelf before.
line @1 react.news.known : That account came round with an earlier lot.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd turn that jar to the light again.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I wish that hurt a shelter from cold tongues.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That news deserves the lid off something good.
line @1 ask.how : Have today's errands sharpened your appetite?
line @1 answer.how : Quiet enough. I'd go a little further if I could.
line @1 sympathise : Stay and share something while your thoughts settle.
line @1 reassure : You needn't fill every empty space at once.
line @1 refuse : I've already promised the free part of my day.
line @1 accept_decline : I'll wrap up the offer without another word.
line @1 preclose : There is a thing still waiting under cloth for me.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go while the path still has its pale edge.
line @1 ack : Aye, that bears looking at.
line @1 thank : You carried the end that would have tipped.
line @2 greet [here.time=dusk] : Welcome as the day's last labels go on.
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# the sealed rim gets my attention before the label. | I leave room between heavy crocks.
b : What is there to see? | For fingers?
a : A gap smaller than a fingernail can waste a week's work. | For a safe grip when the shelf's grown crowded.

scene exchange2
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm bread does my first tasting for me. | I break a hot loaf across the wide bit.
b : Bread has a tongue? | Who gets the soft heart?
a : A plain slice reveals the flavour I've preserved. | I split that between the wolves waiting beside it.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take the longest walk my supper hour allows. | On a walk I count the pauses between carts.
b : How long's that? | To know the time?
a : Out until the noise falls back and home while the light lasts. | To hear when my head has quieted down.

scene exchange4
when topic=home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My count starts after I've set one portion aside. | I store the plainest food nearest my hand.
b : What if your own shelf looks thin? | For everyday eating?
a : Then I know the true length of it. | For a useful share when a hungry visitor comes.

scene exchange5
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh snow looks finer against dark charcoal. | I like fresh flakes still untouched by cart wheels.
b : Why charcoal? | Unspoilt road?
a : It draws every soft white edge as plain as writing. | A chance to hear my own boots travel.

scene exchange6
when topic=day self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cover my tea when a jar wants attention. | I refuse to count cold tea as a drink.
b : Does it keep hot? | What is it then?
a : Longer than my memory usually lasts. | A perfectly clear signal to put the kettle on.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind gets through a cloth cover. | I turn my open jar away from the Sound.
b : Can you taste it? | Afraid of the gulls?
a : Particularly when I've spent good time keeping a batch sweet. | Mostly a breeze that seasons without asking.

scene exchange8
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.friend# the jar with no label. | I can walk beside a friend without filling every pause.
b : Why that one? | Does that cheer you?
a : A friend knows my best share isn't always the smartest dressed. | There's space then for the quiet I came seeking.

scene exchange9
when topic=work self.boss
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I show #self.boss# a bad seal before the tally goes up. | I like an order that says how many usable jars.
b : Even a single one? | Isn't that plain?
a : It's a whole jar to whoever might receive it. | Counting full containers and counting sound food are different matters.

scene exchange10
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I miss how quiet a charcoal stack can be. | A dark patch on snow puts me back in the hills.
b : Quiet with all that burning? | A bad memory?
a : A good slow burn has less to say than one market cart. | It's a place I still carry with some tenderness.

scene exchange11
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard the claim #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | No House seal turns a confidence into common stock.
b : How firm a claim? | Would you repeat it?
a : A label delivered without the jar itself. | Only the part I've proper cause to know.

scene exchange12
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I start a lean week by counting the edible stock. | A poor supper's better when the bread is warm.
b : What else might count? | Does heat cost much?
a : Empty crocks take just as much room on a shelf. | Less if two meals share an oven.

scene exchange13
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The sound of the Sump changes when the wind turns uphill. | The view over a low roof can still hold a hill.
b : What do you hear? | Which bit do you see?
a : The carts more clearly and the water a little less. | A narrow dark line worth lifting my eyes for.

scene exchange14
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I offer a new arrival bread before asking for news. | A stranger can have the spare portion.
b : Why feed first? | May the jar go too?
a : My welcome shouldn't have a price in stories. | An ordinary jar, yes. I'd like the shelf seen from that side.

scene exchange15
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd welcome a shelf still full after I've given something away. | I'd take a jar of fruit up to the old camp.
b : How full? | A present?
a : Enough to carry on sharing through a turn in the weather. | An errand that lets me enjoy the hill in both directions.

scene exchange16
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lid that held through winter calls for gratitude. | A blessing spoken over bread should reach the last slice.
b : Is that a large matter? | How can it reach so far?
a : Ask a hungry stomach how large it feels. | Pass the bread along while it still tastes fresh.

scene exchange17
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I look at the weight after the crock's empty. | A fine label can double a seller's asking price.
b : Why afterwards? | Does it improve the fruit?
a : So next time I know how much dinner the price actually buys. | It would have to be made of remarkable paper.

scene exchange18
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lift a full jar against my apron. | Walking uphill steadies me after a low day.
b : Why so close? | Even in snow?
a : My back has a sensible objection to long arguments with gravity. | Fresh snow gives my feet an extra reason to go carefully.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : At a charcoal camp I learnt that a nearly silent stack could still be at work.
  : Later I stood listening to a shelf of cooling jars and recognised the same slow patience.
  b : Do the jars make a sound?
  : A little click when a lid draws down. The quiet afterwards is what I like.

story tale2 [topic=home self.likes=full_larder]
  : I once wrote the name of a share I'd given away on a label for its empty shelf space.
  : It looked oddly full each time my eye reached the label.
  b : Did you put another crock there?
  : As soon as I could. The label came off with it and made a decent wrapping tie.

story tale3 [topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks]
  : I turned uphill with a warm loaf wrapped against my side.
  : By the last steep turn I'd eaten one end and could feel the other still giving heat.
  b : Did you get back before it cooled?
  : I gave the last piece away warm. That seemed quite as good a finish to the walk.

rule @call1
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say First lid gets a clean wipe. | Morning light along the shelf.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the crocks cool in peace. | Room left for tomorrow's portion.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry your hands on the lifting side. | Mind the wet shelf edge.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wrap the spare before the light goes. | Tea first, labels afterwards.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Our voices can travel here without jarring all the crocks.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I recognise you even across a crowded shelf.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : A House mark doesn't grant a look inside a private cupboard. Give me your question plainly.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.workplace] : My hours at #self.workplace# go into keeping stock sound. A good seal ought to mean the same thing on a rich table as on a poor one.
dlg @2 resident.job : I attend to whatever stock's in reach and leave something for the next meal.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The public word that reached this shelf was #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The label on the story reads #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The rest is still under wrap.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Have a warm bite before the next wind off the water.
graft resident.hub
choice Why count the shelf after taking a jar off it? -> outgoing_jar
node outgoing_jar
say Because the one I've undertaken to give away is no longer part of my supper. It deserves to be counted where it can actually feed somebody.
free
choice What if a stranger needs the next one? -> outgoing_jar_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node outgoing_jar_again
say I'll have a plain look at my cupboard and answer honestly. Nobody needs to wear my House colours to come away with a share.
choice I hope it reaches a hungry table. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
